KaadzOS user Sway overrides
===========================

The generated /etc/skel/.config/sway/config ends with:

    include ~/.config/sway/config.d/*.conf

Files matching *.conf in this directory are read after the generated config,
so they can add bindings, input rules or output settings without editing the
theme output (which theme/generate.sh overwrites).

The KaadzOS settings application writes its overrides here:

    10-wallpaper.conf   output * bg "..." fill
    20-keyboard.conf    input type:keyboard { xkb_layout ... }
    20-touchpad.conf    input type:touchpad { tap ... }

Keep one directive per file and use `swaymsg reload` after a manual edit.
Only *.conf is loaded; this README and backup files stay inert.
